To get started you need Cargo's bin directory (/data/.cargo/bin) in your PATH
environment variable. This has not been done automatically.

To configure your current shell, you need to source
the corresponding env file under /data/.cargo.

This is usually done by running one of the following (note the leading DOT):
. "/data/.cargo/env"            # For sh/bash/zsh/ash/dash/pdksh
source "/data/.cargo/env.fish"  # For fish
source "/data/.cargo/env.nu"  # For nushell
source "/data/.cargo/env.tcsh"  # For tcsh
. "/data/.cargo/env.ps1"        # For pwsh
